<code>assert !this.isEmpty() => \result == this.peekLast();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !this.isEmpty() => this.getLast() == last.item;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !this.isEmpty() => \result == this.getLast();</code>

However, the comment suggests a condition that seems redundant because `getLast()` itself throws a `NoSuchElementException` if the list is empty. Therefore, the assertion should reflect that the result is the last element of the list when the list is not empty. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert !this.isEmpty() => \result == this.peekLast();</code>

This ensures that if the list is not empty, the result of `getLast()` is indeed the last element of the list, which can also be obtained using `peekLast()`.
